WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:10.927
Subtitles are color-coded by country,
and this setting cannot be changed.

2
00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:15.473
The last country
advancing to the final quest is…

3
00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:29.446
…Team Mongolia.

4
00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.323
…Team Mongolia.

5
00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:43.376
We've made the final quest
of Physical: Asia.

6
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.794
It's phenomenal.

7
00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:48.882
My teammates have worked so hard for this.

8
00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:50.550
I'm truly grateful to them.

9
00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:52.594
Game over.

10
00:00:53.845 --> 00:00:55.764
It's all thanks to your awesome idea.

11
00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:01.019
Team Mongolia's finishing time

12
00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:03.646
is 25 minutes and 15 seconds.

13
00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.775
-We were a bit behind.
-It was 25 minutes and 15 seconds.

14
00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:08.568
…Team Mongolia.

15
00:01:11.654 --> 00:01:12.864
That's too bad.

16
00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.742
It is what it is.

17
00:01:20.997 --> 00:01:22.040
Team Japan…

18
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.462
was unable to complete the quest

19
00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:29.297
and is therefore eliminated.

20
00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.674
They didn't complete it?

21
00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.176
What?

22
00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:37.430
-They didn't close the gate.
-They must not have pulled up the bridge.

23
00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:43.561
-Man, I'm frustrated.
-It is what it is. We did our best.

24
00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:47.023
One, two.

25
00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.236
-Shit.
-What's going on?

26
00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:52.487
What's going on?

27
00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.616
It was stuck halfway up and wouldn't move.

28
00:01:56.699 --> 00:02:00.078
No matter how hard we pulled,
it wouldn't budge a single millimeter.

29
00:02:00.161 --> 00:02:01.371
Try jumping and pulling.

30
00:02:03.706 --> 00:02:05.416
-What's going on?
-Maybe this isn't it?

31
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.752
How are we supposed to close it further?

32
00:02:07.836 --> 00:02:09.462
-One, two!
-Two!

33
00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:16.427
We pulled with
every last bit of strength in us.

34
00:02:28.898 --> 00:02:31.568
Regardless, the clock continued to tick.

35
00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:34.070
Man, it's not budging at all.

36
00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:38.241
We were panicking.

37
00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.910
We were completely stumped.

38
00:02:41.786 --> 00:02:42.954
It's coming up a bit!

39
00:02:43.037 --> 00:02:46.332
The thought that we might end up
failing the quest crossed my mind.

40
00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:51.254
Five minutes. That's all we've got.

41
00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:53.590
We're not giving up. Let's keep trying.

42
00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.550
-One, two!
-Let's show them our grit!

43
00:02:58.469 --> 00:02:59.596
It's not moving.

44
00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.056
Keep pulling till the end!

45
00:03:14.068 --> 00:03:15.486
Game over.

46
00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:30.209
-We did everything we could.
-Yeah, it couldn't be helped.

47
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.630
-Well done.
-Good effort. You okay?

48
00:03:34.672 --> 00:03:36.674
-Thanks.
-Thank you.

49
00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:38.009
We ended up

50
00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:43.890
getting timed out
before closing the drawbridge.

51
00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.684
The limitations of my strength

52
00:03:47.352 --> 00:03:49.646
really hit me hard in that moment.

53
00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.564
As the team leader,

54
00:03:51.648 --> 00:03:56.236
I felt frustrated and powerless.

55
00:04:00.531 --> 00:04:02.242
Physical: Asia.

56
00:04:03.493 --> 00:04:07.080
Team Japan has been eliminated
from Physical: Asia.

57
00:04:07.163 --> 00:04:10.959
Each team member
will now destroy their torso.

58
00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.423
The Korea-Japan showdown never came to be.

59
00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.970
We came here aiming to win,

60
00:04:22.053 --> 00:04:25.723
and we were confident
of our victory in Physical: Asia.

61
00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:27.058
Good job!

62
00:04:27.141 --> 00:04:27.976
Thank you!

63
00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:40.280
But Team Japan stands here defeated.

64
00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:46.202
Regardless,
we will rise above this defeat.

65
00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:50.164
It was an honor
to fight beside you all as your leader.

66
00:04:50.248 --> 00:04:51.708
I thank you with all my heart.

67
00:04:59.507 --> 00:05:02.135
Everyone showed such faith in me.

68
00:05:04.053 --> 00:05:05.096
Looking good, Nonoka.

69
00:05:05.179 --> 00:05:06.931
-Come on!
-You got this.

70
00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:12.020
Being on Physical: Asia
taught me for the first time

71
00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:16.899
that I'm not alone,
and I will always treasure my time here.

72
00:05:27.243 --> 00:05:29.662
It's a huge disappointment
to leave like this.

73
00:05:31.372 --> 00:05:34.042
A lot has happened during this experience,

74
00:05:34.125 --> 00:05:39.088
and it's thanks to my teammates
that I could keep going without giving up.

75
00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:43.801
I'm certain
that I came out of this stronger.

76
00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:49.640
We were, without a doubt,
the best team here.

77
00:05:50.433 --> 00:05:54.937
I would like to thank Physical: Asia

78
00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.023
for such a thrilling experience.

79
00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:04.947
I had an amazing time.

80
00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:06.866
I surpassed my limits.

81
00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:10.161
That baseball guy was incredible.

82
00:06:10.995 --> 00:06:12.080
He was amazing.

83
00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:17.210
It's gut-wrenching to leave like this,
but a true battle of physicality is…

84
00:06:20.671 --> 00:06:21.672
Nice!

85
00:06:22.465 --> 00:06:23.466
Push him.

86
00:06:24.759 --> 00:06:25.843
…an awe-inspiring

87
00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.304
and beautiful thing.

88
00:06:33.184 --> 00:06:34.894
-That's it!
-That's it, that's it!

89
00:06:37.021 --> 00:06:39.023
My experience here
was another reminder of that.

90
00:06:39.816 --> 00:06:40.858
Gamsahamnida.

91
00:06:41.651 --> 00:06:43.861
Even his speech is eloquent.

92
00:06:47.532 --> 00:06:48.866
-Right, he's a baseball player.
-Yeah.

93
00:06:54.997 --> 00:06:57.792
The six of us gave it our all.

94
00:07:00.378 --> 00:07:04.674
We fought side by side on Physical: Asia
under the Japanese flag.

95
00:07:07.468 --> 00:07:11.013
We've become more like family
than teammates,

96
00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:13.516
so I kind of feel…

97
00:07:18.688 --> 00:07:22.692
It feels like a huge void
has been left in my heart.

98
00:07:23.526 --> 00:07:25.528
I miss them already.

99
00:07:27.155 --> 00:07:29.699
Despite everything,
it was a privilege to be part of the team.

100
00:07:31.534 --> 00:07:33.035
We fought with everything we had.

101
00:07:34.745 --> 00:07:38.291
So we'll be returning to Japan
with our heads held high.

102
00:07:38.374 --> 00:07:39.208
One, two, three!

103
00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.543
-Go, Japan!
-Go, Japan!

104
00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:41.669
-Go, Japan!
-Go, Japan!

105
00:07:41.752 --> 00:07:42.879
-Go, Japan!
-Go, Japan!

106
00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:51.846
Attention! Bow!

107
00:07:51.929 --> 00:07:52.889
Bow!

108
00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:00.730
-Thank you!
-Thank you.

109
00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:01.898
-Gamsahamnida.
-Thank you.

110
00:08:05.735 --> 00:08:07.361
-Thanks, Dong-hyun.
-Okami.

111
00:08:07.445 --> 00:08:10.656
This is sad.
I wish you all the best in the final.

112
00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:13.951
-Thank you! Nice fight!
-Good job.

113
00:08:14.035 --> 00:08:15.578
-Gamsahamnida.
-Thank you.

114
00:08:44.649 --> 00:08:48.611
PHYSICAL: ASIA

115
00:08:50.196 --> 00:08:54.867
12. ALL-OUT BATTLE

116
00:09:00.122 --> 00:09:00.957
What's going on here?

117
00:09:01.958 --> 00:09:03.376
So this is what I was smelling.

118
00:09:03.459 --> 00:09:04.502
What's this?

119
00:09:05.461 --> 00:09:07.338
We're in for a feast.

120
00:09:07.421 --> 00:09:08.339
Nice.

121
00:09:10.675 --> 00:09:13.844
-It's a feast!
-This looks amazing.

122
00:09:14.387 --> 00:09:16.013
-Are those Mongolian food?
-Yeah, I think so.

123
00:09:16.097 --> 00:09:17.098
Oh, Mongolian food.

124
00:09:18.432 --> 00:09:22.353
When our team makes it to the final,
we're going to make khorkhog.

125
00:09:22.436 --> 00:09:24.981
I want boiled beef and things like buuz.

126
00:09:25.064 --> 00:09:26.607
They're dishes I like.

127
00:09:26.691 --> 00:09:27.525
Goulash!

128
00:09:28.401 --> 00:09:30.027
-Are those Mongolian food?
-You have to try it.

129
00:09:30.111 --> 00:09:31.654
-This one's called buuz.
-Is it delicious?

130
00:09:31.737 --> 00:09:32.655
It's delicious.

131
00:09:34.615 --> 00:09:36.826
-That's khorkhog. Yeah, khorkhog.
-Khorkhog.

132
00:09:38.703 --> 00:09:41.163
Food puts a smile on my face.

133
00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:42.873
These must be Korean dishes.

134
00:09:45.418 --> 00:09:46.877
What would I want for the last meal?

135
00:09:46.961 --> 00:09:49.088
-I'd want ginseng chicken soup.
-A nice bowl of pot rice.

136
00:09:49.171 --> 00:09:51.924
I think I'd want pork belly
and kimchi stew.

137
00:09:52.008 --> 00:09:54.719
-Look at that braised kimchi and pork!
-That looks good.

138
00:09:54.802 --> 00:09:56.053
They've gota soup of boiled chicken!

139
00:09:56.554 --> 00:09:57.722
That looks good.

140
00:10:02.643 --> 00:10:04.687
Look at that. They've prepared pot rice.

141
00:10:06.147 --> 00:10:07.690
It reminded me of The Last Supper.

142
00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:11.402
Whenever someone gets a fancy meal
in movies or dramas

143
00:10:11.485 --> 00:10:12.862
they usually end up dead.

144
00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:13.904
Bon appétit.

145
00:10:14.614 --> 00:10:16.741
-Enjoy.
-Enjoy.

146
00:10:19.368 --> 00:10:23.247
I was thrilled to have Mongolian food
before going into the final.

147
00:10:23.331 --> 00:10:26.292
It filled me with motivation and energy.

148
00:10:30.671 --> 00:10:34.675
Thinking about it, it was kind of funny
that we were sharing a meal

149
00:10:34.759 --> 00:10:38.095
with our rival team just before the match.

150
00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:42.099
The lamb's tasty.

151
00:10:46.103 --> 00:10:47.271
The lamb's really good.

152
00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.281
Eat up, guys.
You're about to get crushed soon.

153
00:10:57.365 --> 00:10:59.867
Eat up, guys.
You're about to get crushed soon.

154
00:11:04.163 --> 00:11:08.292
While we were eating,
the battle of nerves had already begun.

155
00:11:08.376 --> 00:11:10.378
I felt their eyes on us,

156
00:11:10.461 --> 00:11:14.465
analyzing how confident
or nervous we were.

157
00:11:15.049 --> 00:11:17.343
I could tell they were observing us.

158
00:11:17.927 --> 00:11:20.679
How do you think
they closed the drawbridge?

159
00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:24.600
I bet they're strong.
They get their strength from kimchi.

160
00:11:24.683 --> 00:11:26.644
Team Mongolia really is strong.

161
00:11:27.686 --> 00:11:30.231
I really didn't expect them
to be in the final.

162
00:11:30.314 --> 00:11:31.273
I didn't either.

163
00:11:32.775 --> 00:11:34.068
Khandsuren.

164
00:11:34.568 --> 00:11:36.862
Did you expect to see us in the final?

165
00:11:36.946 --> 00:11:37.947
Did you see it coming?

166
00:11:38.864 --> 00:11:41.325
I knew you guys would win.
We expected to meet you here.

167
00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:48.833
What was your take?
Did you think we were going to win?

168
00:11:48.916 --> 00:11:50.543
-What was their take?
-Their take?

169
00:11:54.004 --> 00:11:56.215
If I'm being honest, no.

170
00:11:56.715 --> 00:11:58.092
I honestly didn't.

171
00:11:58.843 --> 00:12:01.429
I thought you guys were just lucky,

172
00:12:01.512 --> 00:12:04.557
but I realize now
that you are a truly strong team.

173
00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:07.685
-They thought we were lucky ducks.
-We are lucky, to be fair.

174
00:12:10.521 --> 00:12:13.607
We were observing Team Korea
throughout the meal.

175
00:12:13.691 --> 00:12:16.360
I made sure not to give myself away
to Team Mongolia.

176
00:12:16.944 --> 00:12:20.906
I could tell Orkhonbayar was thinking
the exact same thing about us.

177
00:12:21.907 --> 00:12:24.702
It's hard to believe that we're eating
facing each other like this,

178
00:12:24.785 --> 00:12:27.413
when a billion won's at stake.

179
00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:31.333
One team will go home empty-handed,
the other with a billion won.

180
00:12:33.335 --> 00:12:36.005
I'm not worried about the match,

181
00:12:36.088 --> 00:12:38.632
but I am a bit worried about
how we'll count all that cash.

182
00:12:42.178 --> 00:12:43.721
They're funny.

183
00:12:43.804 --> 00:12:45.931
They were counting their chickens,

184
00:12:47.308 --> 00:12:49.059
when we were going to be the victors.

185
00:12:49.894 --> 00:12:51.395
What would you do with the prize money?

186
00:12:51.979 --> 00:12:54.982
If we were to win the match
and the prize money,

187
00:12:55.065 --> 00:12:57.735
we'll spend it to invite you over
on a trip to Mongolia.

188
00:12:57.818 --> 00:13:00.404
…we'll spend it to invite you to over
on a trip to Mongolia.

189
00:13:03.282 --> 00:13:04.116
I'm touched.

190
00:13:04.742 --> 00:13:07.369
Now let's give it our all
in this final match.

191
00:13:07.912 --> 00:13:09.079
Let's leave no regrets.

192
00:13:13.959 --> 00:13:15.544
Let's make this an epic finale.

193
00:13:16.045 --> 00:13:19.131
I'm pumped because I think
it'll be a very close match.

194
00:13:19.215 --> 00:13:21.759
As for the trip to Mongolia you mentioned,

195
00:13:21.842 --> 00:13:24.094
we're totally down to visit you
with our winnings.

196
00:13:24.178 --> 00:13:26.555
…we're totally down to visit you
with our winnings.

197
00:13:34.188 --> 00:13:37.441
The final quest of Physical: Asia.

198
00:13:37.525 --> 00:13:39.485
Damn, we've made it to the final quest.

199
00:13:40.486 --> 00:13:44.073
Contestants,
please make your way to the arena.

200
00:13:44.657 --> 00:13:46.242
All right. Here we go.

201
00:13:46.325 --> 00:13:47.409
All right!

202
00:13:47.993 --> 00:13:49.286
It's the final quest.

203
00:14:17.356 --> 00:14:19.024
Physical: Asia.

204
00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:23.988
Contestants of
Teams Republic of Korea and Mongolia,

205
00:14:24.071 --> 00:14:26.365
please enter the arena
for the final quest.

206
00:14:32.371 --> 00:14:34.748
-Man, what's this?
-What's this?

207
00:14:35.833 --> 00:14:37.751
-It's a track.
-There's a track.

208
00:14:39.587 --> 00:14:42.006
-There's a track.
-I guess we'll be running.

209
00:14:42.089 --> 00:14:43.132
There's a box.

210
00:14:44.967 --> 00:14:47.344
It looks like
we're going to be pushing those.

211
00:14:47.928 --> 00:14:50.639
We walked into a huge circular track

212
00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:52.850
with three large boxes.

213
00:14:53.684 --> 00:14:56.103
We'll probably have to
push those boxes, right?

214
00:14:56.186 --> 00:14:57.187
I think so.

215
00:14:57.271 --> 00:14:59.064
There are balls over there too.

216
00:15:00.691 --> 00:15:02.693
There's rope and a metal ball.

217
00:15:03.819 --> 00:15:07.364
Look at all those clips on it.
Maybe we have to pull it over there?

218
00:15:07.448 --> 00:15:08.282
You're right.

219
00:15:09.867 --> 00:15:11.076
I have no clue.

220
00:15:11.577 --> 00:15:12.995
-I have no clue what the quest will be.
-Right.

221
00:15:14.204 --> 00:15:15.414
I can't figure it out.

222
00:15:17.666 --> 00:15:22.546
I thought there'd only be one game,

223
00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.466
but there were lots of different objects.

224
00:15:25.549 --> 00:15:30.220
There was a ball-like object,
a wall on one side,

225
00:15:30.304 --> 00:15:33.682
a track, and a whole lot of
different objects.

226
00:15:33.766 --> 00:15:36.602
The setup looked fitting
for games worthy of a final.

227
00:15:40.898 --> 00:15:45.402
The two countries that have
made it through to the final quest

228
00:15:46.528 --> 00:15:47.529
are Team Republic of Korea…

229
00:15:49.615 --> 00:15:50.616
and Team Mongolia.

230
00:15:53.202 --> 00:15:55.496
Only the one country
that demonstrates exceptional teamwork

231
00:15:55.579 --> 00:15:58.582
to survive until the end

232
00:15:59.208 --> 00:16:03.504
will be crowned the country
that embodies the most perfect physique.

233
00:16:05.839 --> 00:16:07.383
The country

234
00:16:07.883 --> 00:16:10.344
that emerges as the champion
of the final quest

235
00:16:11.845 --> 00:16:12.846
will win…

236
00:16:15.849 --> 00:16:17.726
one billion won.

237
00:16:18.644 --> 00:16:20.521
…one billion won.

238
00:16:23.524 --> 00:16:25.693
Of course the prize money is important.

239
00:16:25.776 --> 00:16:27.778
But the honor of winning

240
00:16:27.861 --> 00:16:31.991
and having South Korea take the top spot
out of eight Asian countries

241
00:16:32.074 --> 00:16:34.201
is what I'm playing for.

242
00:16:34.284 --> 00:16:37.997
I want to bring home a win for Mongolia.

243
00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:41.000
This win has to be ours.

244
00:16:41.834 --> 00:16:43.419
Here's a final speech

245
00:16:43.502 --> 00:16:46.046
from Team Leader of the Republic of Korea,
Kim Dong-hyun.

246
00:16:48.757 --> 00:16:53.262
As I said in my first speech
on Physical: Asia,

247
00:16:53.345 --> 00:16:56.724
I believe that physical ability
stems from the mind.

248
00:16:56.807 --> 00:17:00.102
And our grit and mental fortitude
are what have carried us this far.

249
00:17:00.185 --> 00:17:01.353
Every step of the way,

250
00:17:01.437 --> 00:17:04.023
we've fought
until we could taste blood in our throats.

251
00:17:04.106 --> 00:17:06.900
This time, we'll fight to the end
until we cough up blood

252
00:17:06.984 --> 00:17:09.611
to demonstrate the strength
that we Koreans have.

253
00:17:11.155 --> 00:17:13.490
I have faith that we'll win this.

254
00:17:13.574 --> 00:17:16.118
We're all strong individually,

255
00:17:16.201 --> 00:17:20.372
but more than that,
we're an incredibly unified team.

256
00:17:20.456 --> 00:17:23.125
In the end, it's our teamwork
that'll lead us to dominate.

257
00:17:25.044 --> 00:17:26.795
Here's a final speech

258
00:17:26.879 --> 00:17:30.799
from Team Leader of Mongolia,
Orkhonbayar Bayarsaikhan.

259
00:17:31.842 --> 00:17:34.219
We've made it this far
by crushing every quest

260
00:17:34.303 --> 00:17:37.056
as a united team with a shared goal.

261
00:17:37.139 --> 00:17:38.974
We came here for nothing but victory.

262
00:17:39.058 --> 00:17:40.309
Therefore,

263
00:17:40.392 --> 00:17:43.353
we'll fight with everything we have
until there's nothing left.

264
00:17:43.437 --> 00:17:44.480
We will win this.

265
00:17:44.563 --> 00:17:45.606
Let's bring it!

266
00:17:48.984 --> 00:17:50.569
We're here for one thing only,

267
00:17:51.904 --> 00:17:53.363
and that's victory.

268
00:17:53.989 --> 00:17:55.657
We'll give it everything we've got.

269
00:17:55.741 --> 00:18:00.829
I hope both teams bring their best
and make this a showdown to remember.

270
00:18:02.873 --> 00:18:08.712
The final quest of Physical: Asia
will now be revealed.

271
00:18:13.217 --> 00:18:14.551
The final quest is…

272
00:18:18.138 --> 00:18:20.390
the six-on-six all-out team match.

273
00:18:21.391 --> 00:18:23.477
All right, this is perfect.

274
00:18:25.979 --> 00:18:28.148
The six-on-six all-out team match…

275
00:18:30.234 --> 00:18:32.319
will consist of a total of three games.

276
00:18:32.402 --> 00:18:34.321
Three? Seriously?

277
00:18:34.404 --> 00:18:35.781
-Let's win all three.
-Three, huh?

278
00:18:35.864 --> 00:18:37.032
-Let's win them all.
-Are we playing them all at once?

279
00:18:37.616 --> 00:18:39.076
All six team members

280
00:18:39.785 --> 00:18:41.120
will participate

281
00:18:42.246 --> 00:18:43.831
in each of the three games.

282
00:18:46.625 --> 00:18:51.755
Going all-out in a six-on-six match
will work to our advantage.

283
00:18:52.339 --> 00:18:57.136
The first country to win
two out of the three games

284
00:18:58.095 --> 00:18:59.555
will be crowned

285
00:19:00.305 --> 00:19:03.016
the final winner of Physical: Asia.

286
00:19:05.102 --> 00:19:06.186
The first game

287
00:19:07.437 --> 00:19:08.564
is the wall-pushing match.

288
00:19:10.691 --> 00:19:11.859
In the wall-pushing match,

289
00:19:11.942 --> 00:19:14.820
the country that pushes the walls
from the center

290
00:19:14.903 --> 00:19:18.740
further into the opponent's zone wins.

291
00:19:18.824 --> 00:19:20.617
It's all about pushing with brute force.

292
00:19:20.701 --> 00:19:23.203
It's a strength game.
Just think of it as a reverse tug-of-war.

293
00:19:23.287 --> 00:19:24.705
It'll be a face-off of brute force.

294
00:19:25.289 --> 00:19:26.331
The second game

295
00:19:27.875 --> 00:19:29.293
is the iron ball dragging match.

296
00:19:31.879 --> 00:19:33.547
In the iron ball dragging match,

297
00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:36.341
all six team members
will drag the iron weights

298
00:19:36.425 --> 00:19:41.138
to the finish point
within the allotted time.

299
00:19:41.889 --> 00:19:45.434
So each team will pull its own
set of weights to the finish point.

300
00:19:47.644 --> 00:19:48.645
The third game…

301
00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:53.233
is the infinite tail tag match.

302
00:19:54.026 --> 00:19:55.777
…the infinite tail tag match.

303
00:19:57.571 --> 00:19:59.489
-That's going to be brutal.
-What is that?

304
00:19:59.573 --> 00:20:01.074
In the infinite tail tag match,

305
00:20:01.617 --> 00:20:03.410
each team will split
into two groups of three

306
00:20:03.493 --> 00:20:05.204
and take turns running.

307
00:20:05.787 --> 00:20:08.832
The team that completely overtakes
the opposing group

308
00:20:08.916 --> 00:20:11.710
starting on the opposite side, wins.

309
00:20:12.211 --> 00:20:15.005
We each start from our starting point

310
00:20:15.088 --> 00:20:18.884
and continue running
until we overtake the opposing group.

311
00:20:18.967 --> 00:20:21.845
This is all about mental strength, guys.

312
00:20:21.929 --> 00:20:24.973
I'm sorry, but you'll get pushed along
if you fall behind.

313
00:20:25.557 --> 00:20:28.727
We need to be ready to run 10 km.
Whichever team is faster will win.

314
00:20:31.521 --> 00:20:32.648
Let's finish this in the second game.

315
00:20:34.858 --> 00:20:37.527
The first game of the three is…

316
00:20:45.744 --> 00:20:46.954
the wall-pushing match.

317
00:20:47.955 --> 00:20:50.999
This is going to test everyone's strength.

318
00:20:52.918 --> 00:20:54.461
-We've got to win this one.
-Yeah.

319
00:20:55.379 --> 00:20:56.630
We need to win at all costs.

320
00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:00.550
I figured we had the upper hand

321
00:21:00.634 --> 00:21:02.094
when it came to the wall-pushing match.

322
00:21:02.177 --> 00:21:05.138
We're obviously much stronger
and that's worked to our advantage

323
00:21:05.222 --> 00:21:06.890
in winning the quests so far.

324
00:21:07.557 --> 00:21:09.184
The second game

325
00:21:09.268 --> 00:21:12.479
will be chosen by the loser
of the first game.

326
00:21:13.647 --> 00:21:16.942
Let's win the first and second games.

327
00:21:17.526 --> 00:21:20.028
All right, the strategy's coming together.

328
00:21:20.112 --> 00:21:20.946
Nice.

329
00:21:21.446 --> 00:21:24.950
The final quest of Physical: Asia.

330
00:21:26.576 --> 00:21:27.911
The first game.

331
00:21:27.995 --> 00:21:29.079
The wall-pushing match.

332
00:21:29.621 --> 00:21:31.832
The game will now begin.

333
00:22:00.444 --> 00:22:02.779
The first game of the final quest.

334
00:22:04.239 --> 00:22:06.908
Here are the rules
of the wall-pushing match.

335
00:22:07.909 --> 00:22:11.371
In this match,
the country that pushes the walls

336
00:22:11.872 --> 00:22:13.165
in the center of the three tracks

337
00:22:14.207 --> 00:22:17.669
further into the opponent's zone wins.

338
00:22:18.337 --> 00:22:20.172
The walls are all different sizes.

339
00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.304
Man, this is going to be a fun match.

340
00:22:29.139 --> 00:22:34.269
You may distribute your six players
across the three tracks,

341
00:22:35.395 --> 00:22:37.731
and move freely between them.

342
00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:41.735
We'll need to keep switching tracks.

343
00:22:41.818 --> 00:22:43.445
We'll have to rack our brains for this.

344
00:22:43.528 --> 00:22:44.738
The game

345
00:22:45.697 --> 00:22:46.782
will last for five minutes.

346
00:22:48.033 --> 00:22:49.409
The country

347
00:22:50.118 --> 00:22:54.748
that wins over more tracks
out of the three will be the winner.

348
00:22:56.875 --> 00:22:57.709
We can't end it then.

349
00:22:57.793 --> 00:22:59.961
We have to keep the walls in their zone
until the time's up.

350
00:23:00.045 --> 00:23:01.088
Is that how it is?

351
00:23:01.963 --> 00:23:05.675
A total of three rounds
will be played the same way,

352
00:23:06.176 --> 00:23:10.097
and the first country to win two rounds
will be the winner.

353
00:23:10.180 --> 00:23:12.099
-Three rounds?
-We're playing three rounds of that?

354
00:23:12.182 --> 00:23:13.475
Come on.

355
00:23:13.975 --> 00:23:14.935
This was going to be tough.

356
00:23:15.018 --> 00:23:20.482
When it comes to pushing,
it doesn't matter how strong you are.

357
00:23:20.565 --> 00:23:23.944
If there's someone of similar strength
pushing against you on the other side,

358
00:23:24.027 --> 00:23:26.279
you're not getting anywhere.

359
00:23:26.363 --> 00:23:28.698
The rules were simple
and easy to understand.

360
00:23:28.782 --> 00:23:33.995
The way to play this was to focus on
getting over two of the three walls.

361
00:23:34.621 --> 00:23:37.040
Please start your strategy meeting.

362
00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:41.253
All right, so here's what I think.

363
00:23:41.336 --> 00:23:46.133
We take on just two of them,
and start with the two heaviest ones.

364
00:23:46.216 --> 00:23:48.844
We split up into
two groups of three, right?

365
00:23:48.927 --> 00:23:52.681
Adiyasuren, Dulguun, and Lkhagva-Ochir
will be in one group.

366
00:23:53.849 --> 00:23:57.686
And the other group
will be Khandsuren, Enkh-Orgil, and me.

367
00:23:57.769 --> 00:23:59.688
Okay, so…

368
00:24:01.022 --> 00:24:04.401
We can play this several different ways,
but here's what I think.

369
00:24:04.484 --> 00:24:07.445
We match a player on the other side
based on weight and follow them around.

370
00:24:07.529 --> 00:24:10.365
So if the bökh guy heads over there,
then you follow him.

371
00:24:10.448 --> 00:24:12.117
Or you could stay here alone,

372
00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:13.660
and two others
move to each side to help out.

373
00:24:13.743 --> 00:24:16.037
How about we just focus on
two of the walls?

374
00:24:16.121 --> 00:24:17.205
-On two of them?
-Yeah.

375
00:24:17.289 --> 00:24:18.874
But what if we're losing on both?

376
00:24:18.957 --> 00:24:20.792
What would we do then?

377
00:24:20.876 --> 00:24:23.879
It would be good to have
the upper hand in the middle one.

378
00:24:23.962 --> 00:24:25.255
Because if we win that one…

379
00:24:25.338 --> 00:24:27.174
Dong-hyun seemed a bit ruffled.

380
00:24:27.257 --> 00:24:31.136
We kept jumping from one idea to the next
without making a decision.

381
00:24:31.761 --> 00:24:35.390
We couldn't seem to settle on an idea.

382
00:24:35.473 --> 00:24:37.058
We weren't any closer to deciding.

383
00:24:38.059 --> 00:24:41.188
The strategy meeting
will be over in one minute.

384
00:24:41.271 --> 00:24:44.399
Let's decide who's going to
start off in the center with Min-jae.

385
00:24:45.567 --> 00:24:46.651
You see…

386
00:24:48.737 --> 00:24:54.326
I'm the kind of person
who has to run through every possibility.

387
00:24:54.409 --> 00:24:59.164
But this wall-pushing match
was impossible to predict.

388
00:25:01.249 --> 00:25:04.544
The final quest of Physical: Asia.

389
00:25:04.628 --> 00:25:06.129
The first game.

390
00:25:06.630 --> 00:25:07.964
The wall-pushing match.

391
00:25:08.048 --> 00:25:10.133
The first round will now begin.

392
00:25:11.051 --> 00:25:12.010
Remember to keep shifting.

393
00:25:12.093 --> 00:25:13.929
-Go straight to your spots, okay?
-Yeah.

394
00:25:14.012 --> 00:25:15.263
-Go as soon as it starts.
-Okay.

395
00:25:17.265 --> 00:25:19.643
We decided to keep it flexible
and pivot when needed.

396
00:25:19.726 --> 00:25:22.395
We figured we had a slight edge
in terms of strength.

397
00:25:25.148 --> 00:25:27.359
-The two on the end are headed there.
-Stand by.

398
00:25:27.943 --> 00:25:29.736
Three of them
will be going for the big one.

399
00:25:29.819 --> 00:25:30.946
Follow me, Adiyasuren.

400
00:25:31.029 --> 00:25:32.030
Ready…

401
00:25:42.624 --> 00:25:43.458
Push!

402
00:25:43.959 --> 00:25:45.543
All right, this is perfect.

403
00:25:45.627 --> 00:25:46.461
I told you.

404
00:25:48.755 --> 00:25:49.714
Push!

405
00:25:50.632 --> 00:25:51.508
There are two of them.

406
00:25:59.224 --> 00:26:00.976
-One, two!
-Two!

407
00:26:01.059 --> 00:26:02.102
One, two!

408
00:26:03.228 --> 00:26:04.437
Push against them.

409
00:26:04.521 --> 00:26:05.605
We're holding our ground.

410
00:26:09.776 --> 00:26:10.735
Okay.

411
00:26:11.695 --> 00:26:12.570
Okay.

412
00:26:12.654 --> 00:26:13.780
Hold your ground.

413
00:26:15.657 --> 00:26:17.242
-Seung-yeon, extend your leg back.
-Further.

414
00:26:17.909 --> 00:26:19.160
They have the same game plan.

415
00:26:23.123 --> 00:26:26.209
-One, two.
-That's it. We ease back when they push.

416
00:26:26.293 --> 00:26:27.836
-One, two, three!
-Two, three!

417
00:26:32.048 --> 00:26:35.051
We figured the middle wall
was the most important.

418
00:26:35.135 --> 00:26:38.430
So that's where we put our strongest guys,
Amotti, Min-jae, and Sung-bin.

419
00:26:38.513 --> 00:26:40.223
We can't just keep holding like this.

420
00:26:40.307 --> 00:26:44.019
The rest of us would take on
the two-unit wall on the left.

421
00:26:44.102 --> 00:26:45.020
But Team Mongolia

422
00:26:45.603 --> 00:26:48.481
did exactly the same thing,
almost as if we had agreed on it.

423
00:26:50.275 --> 00:26:52.152
Hold your ground, guys. You have the edge.

424
00:26:52.652 --> 00:26:54.696
-They're in our zone, aren't they?
-Yeah, a bit.

425
00:26:56.197 --> 00:26:57.240
One, two, three!

426
00:26:58.199 --> 00:26:59.576
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three!

427
00:26:59.659 --> 00:27:00.744
One, two, three.

428
00:27:01.244 --> 00:27:04.164
Don't push too hard.
Just hold it while those guys are pushing.

429
00:27:04.247 --> 00:27:06.624
-We'll push when they gas out.
-Okay, we push then.

430
00:27:06.708 --> 00:27:08.960
-Okay. One, two, three, push!
-One, two, three. That's it!

431
00:27:09.044 --> 00:27:11.629
-Okay. One, two, three, push!
-One, two, three. That's it!

432
00:27:11.713 --> 00:27:13.214
We're pushing hard right now.

433
00:27:13.923 --> 00:27:14.758
Let's keep holding.

434
00:27:14.841 --> 00:27:16.968
We can't just keep holding like this.
We've got to push back.

435
00:27:17.052 --> 00:27:18.595
-One, two, three!
-One, two!

436
00:27:18.678 --> 00:27:19.679
One, two!

437
00:27:20.722 --> 00:27:21.848
-One, two!
-One, two!

438
00:27:21.931 --> 00:27:23.308
Now! Push now!

439
00:27:23.975 --> 00:27:25.477
-One, two!
-One, two, three!

440
00:27:25.977 --> 00:27:26.853
That's it!

441
00:27:26.936 --> 00:27:28.480
Okay, hold it here now.

442
00:27:28.563 --> 00:27:30.315
-One, two, three!
-Holding it!

443
00:27:32.901 --> 00:27:34.944
Team Mongolia had a girl on their side,

444
00:27:35.028 --> 00:27:38.323
so I assumed we'd totally outmuscle them.

445
00:27:38.406 --> 00:27:41.659
But we were getting pushed back
little by little.

446
00:27:41.743 --> 00:27:44.371
We should've been
overpowering them with ease.

447
00:27:45.372 --> 00:27:48.958
I was amazed by Adiyasuren's strength.

448
00:27:54.923 --> 00:27:56.216
One, two!

449
00:27:56.299 --> 00:27:58.009
-We're not coordinated right now.
-You're right.

450
00:28:00.762 --> 00:28:01.805
Keep holding.

451
00:28:03.181 --> 00:28:04.516
-We're in their zone.
-Yeah?

452
00:28:04.599 --> 00:28:06.309
Okay, are you ready to push a bit?

453
00:28:06.393 --> 00:28:07.977
-One, two!
-One, two!

454
00:28:09.145 --> 00:28:09.979
That's it!

455
00:28:11.356 --> 00:28:12.690
-That's it!
-Again!

456
00:28:12.774 --> 00:28:13.983
-We're getting pushed back.
-Yeah.

457
00:28:14.776 --> 00:28:15.693
Let's give it a shove.

458
00:28:16.277 --> 00:28:17.445
One, two, three!

459
00:28:18.530 --> 00:28:19.948
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three, push!

460
00:28:20.031 --> 00:28:21.408
-One, two, three!
-Push!

461
00:28:21.491 --> 00:28:22.617
One, two, three!

462
00:28:23.660 --> 00:28:24.953
It's not budging.

463
00:28:27.414 --> 00:28:29.499
The five minutes
were counting down quickly.

464
00:28:29.999 --> 00:28:32.127
We were on the back foot,
just trying to hold them off.

465
00:28:32.210 --> 00:28:33.795
We needed to change tack.

466
00:28:34.295 --> 00:28:37.132
-Dong-hyun, that wall's clear for now.
-Right.

467
00:28:37.215 --> 00:28:38.842
Why don't we go for that one right now?

468
00:28:38.925 --> 00:28:39.926
Hold on.

469
00:28:40.009 --> 00:28:41.970
-Let's go and push that into their zone.
-What?

470
00:28:42.053 --> 00:28:42.971
Let's go for it.

471
00:28:43.471 --> 00:28:44.556
The third one.

472
00:28:46.015 --> 00:28:49.769
I think she's saying,
"Check the time and stay still."

473
00:28:50.353 --> 00:28:51.688
One, two, three.

474
00:28:51.771 --> 00:28:53.732
It really felt like
we were pushing a wall.

475
00:28:53.815 --> 00:28:55.150
They were strong as hell.

476
00:28:56.317 --> 00:29:00.613
I was panicking
because I couldn't figure out what to do.

477
00:29:02.782 --> 00:29:03.783
Should we go now?

478
00:29:03.867 --> 00:29:05.160
Should we go on the count of three?

479
00:29:05.243 --> 00:29:07.454
-Are all three of us going?
-Yeah, all of us.

480
00:29:07.537 --> 00:29:10.081
Maybe one person should stay behind
while the other two go?

481
00:29:10.165 --> 00:29:11.207
No.

482
00:29:11.291 --> 00:29:13.042
-We'll go together at three minutes.
-All right.

483
00:29:13.126 --> 00:29:14.794
-Are all of us going?
-Yeah, in three seconds.

484
00:29:14.878 --> 00:29:16.463
-Three, two, one. Go!
-Two, one. Go!

485
00:29:16.546 --> 00:29:17.380
Go!

486
00:29:17.964 --> 00:29:19.924
-One, go!
-Go!

487
00:29:24.012 --> 00:29:26.848
Okay, push.
Just push it all the way to the end.

488
00:29:29.476 --> 00:29:30.310
Push!

489
00:29:31.936 --> 00:29:32.896
-We got it.
-I'll hold fort here.

490
00:29:32.979 --> 00:29:34.856
-Go and help them.
-Okay.

491
00:29:34.939 --> 00:29:36.107
You go with him, Seung-yeon.

492
00:29:37.108 --> 00:29:38.151
Now come here.

493
00:29:38.234 --> 00:29:41.154
I was watching Team Korea very carefully.

494
00:29:41.780 --> 00:29:45.492
We completely ruled out the first track

495
00:29:45.575 --> 00:29:49.537
and stuck to our plan
of focusing on the other two.

496
00:29:51.706 --> 00:29:52.540
Now come here.

497
00:29:57.045 --> 00:29:58.713
One, two, three.

498
00:29:58.797 --> 00:30:02.175
-One, two, three!
-That's it!

499
00:30:02.258 --> 00:30:04.135
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three. Yes!

500
00:30:04.219 --> 00:30:05.887
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three. Yes!

501
00:30:06.471 --> 00:30:08.515
-One, two, three!
-One, two!

502
00:30:08.598 --> 00:30:10.475
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three!

503
00:30:31.913 --> 00:30:34.207
Seung-yeon! Seung-yeon!

504
00:30:34.290 --> 00:30:35.625
One of you, go over there!

505
00:30:35.708 --> 00:30:37.043
One of you, go over there!

