-We need to let Min-jae lead.
-Yeah, that's right.

755
00:43:05.833 --> 00:43:09.169
We were beat, completely gassed,
and mentally drained.

756
00:43:09.253 --> 00:43:12.423
But now that we were
in the position of the predator,

757
00:43:13.090 --> 00:43:14.633
I was having an absolute blast.

758
00:43:14.717 --> 00:43:18.137
I wanted this win so bad,
I was ready to wreck myself completely.

759
00:43:18.220 --> 00:43:20.764
I wanted to drive those boxes
straight through our opponent.

760
00:43:22.349 --> 00:43:24.476
They're not going to ignore
the single-unit wall this time.

761
00:43:24.560 --> 00:43:26.270
-I'll still go to it though.
-Yeah? Okay.

762
00:43:26.353 --> 00:43:29.023
-You should, since you're the fastest.
-Yeah, it's best if I go.

763
00:43:29.106 --> 00:43:31.442
You go back to your first spot
in the center.

764
00:43:31.942 --> 00:43:35.195
We'd just won with an awesome strategy,
so there was no need to change it up.

765
00:43:35.279 --> 00:43:37.656
We've got Sung-bin
who's faster than anyone,

766
00:43:37.740 --> 00:43:40.534
and if Min-jae
and the rest of us go all out,

767
00:43:40.618 --> 00:43:41.952
we were sure to win.

768
00:43:42.453 --> 00:43:44.913
-Why did you lose the center?
-You just had to hold out.

769
00:43:45.497 --> 00:43:47.333
They're striking when you guys are gassed.

770
00:43:47.416 --> 00:43:50.336
Brace yourself like this,
and use your knee for support.

771
00:43:51.587 --> 00:43:54.006
Of course I was bummed out about the loss.

772
00:43:54.506 --> 00:43:56.884
We tried to shut down
Team Korea's strong offensive

773
00:43:56.967 --> 00:44:01.513
from where we were standing,
but it didn't work out.

774
00:44:03.182 --> 00:44:07.478
We came up with a tactic
for the third round.

775
00:44:07.561 --> 00:44:10.314
We're going to try to weaken
Team Korea as much as possible

776
00:44:10.397 --> 00:44:11.940
by spreading out all over.

777
00:44:12.024 --> 00:44:13.776
I think we're going to win this one.

778
00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:19.198
The first game of the final quest.

779
00:44:19.281 --> 00:44:20.240
The wall-pushing match.

780
00:44:21.992 --> 00:44:25.079
The third and final round will now begin.

781
00:44:30.417 --> 00:44:31.502
Stand by.

782
00:44:34.254 --> 00:44:35.214
Ready…

783
00:44:42.304 --> 00:44:43.180
Ram it!

784
00:44:52.773 --> 00:44:54.316
Yes, we got it.

785
00:44:54.400 --> 00:44:56.193
-Okay, they're holding over there.
-One, two!

786
00:44:57.152 --> 00:44:58.070
-One, two!
-One, two!

787
00:44:58.821 --> 00:45:01.115
My job was to do whatever I could

788
00:45:01.198 --> 00:45:04.993
to stop Sung-bin
from backing up the middle track.

789
00:45:05.077 --> 00:45:06.036
But…

790
00:45:09.248 --> 00:45:10.124
One, two!

791
00:45:10.958 --> 00:45:11.917
One, two!

792
00:45:12.751 --> 00:45:13.627
One, two!

793
00:45:14.378 --> 00:45:15.254
-One, two!
-One, two!

794
00:45:16.046 --> 00:45:16.964
-One, two!
-One, two!

795
00:45:17.714 --> 00:45:18.632
-One, two!
-One, two!

796
00:45:19.466 --> 00:45:21.135
He's going! Go, Sung-bin!

797
00:45:38.819 --> 00:45:40.779
All we had to do was hold our positions.

798
00:45:40.863 --> 00:45:41.989
This was impossible to lose.

799
00:45:43.407 --> 00:45:45.659
Hold it, hold it. Okay.

800
00:45:46.160 --> 00:45:47.661
Let's push now. Two, three.

801
00:45:50.664 --> 00:45:54.543
Sung-bin firmly held his ground
as we'd planned,

802
00:45:54.626 --> 00:45:57.754
and Min-jae also held his ground
in the center track.

803
00:45:58.464 --> 00:46:01.967
This time, we focused a bit more
on defense and on reading the situation.

804
00:46:03.135 --> 00:46:06.054
Hold it, hold it!

805
00:46:06.889 --> 00:46:09.516
Hold it, hold it.

806
00:46:11.393 --> 00:46:14.229
Come on. Come over here.

807
00:46:14.313 --> 00:46:15.147
One, two, three.

808
00:46:15.898 --> 00:46:17.649
One, two, three.

809
00:46:17.733 --> 00:46:18.859
One, two, three.

810
00:46:19.359 --> 00:46:20.194
I'll go.

811
00:46:20.277 --> 00:46:22.404
-No, you go, Eun-sil.
-Go, Dong-hyun.

812
00:46:22.488 --> 00:46:23.322
I'll go.

813
00:46:24.281 --> 00:46:26.575
Come here. It's all right.

814
00:46:26.658 --> 00:46:28.452
Come and push.

815
00:46:28.535 --> 00:46:29.995
One, two… Sung-bin. One, two.

816
00:46:30.787 --> 00:46:31.705
-One, two.
-One, two.

817
00:46:32.456 --> 00:46:35.334
-One, two…
-Stay in place and hold out!

818
00:46:35.417 --> 00:46:37.628
-One, two, three.
-Stay in place and hold out.

819
00:46:39.213 --> 00:46:40.214
One, two!

820
00:46:41.089 --> 00:46:41.924
One, two.

821
00:46:42.966 --> 00:46:43.842
One, two.

822
00:46:45.719 --> 00:46:46.970
-Let's push.
-Okay.

823
00:46:47.054 --> 00:46:49.431
Get lower.
Sung-bin, try pushing further in.

824
00:46:49.515 --> 00:46:50.682
They're weak on that one.

825
00:46:50.766 --> 00:46:51.892
All right.

826
00:46:51.975 --> 00:46:53.519
-Dig in, dig in.
-Let's dig in.

827
00:46:54.102 --> 00:46:56.396
Let's dig in
and push against them on their count.

828
00:46:56.480 --> 00:46:58.357
-One, two!
-Let's just hold for now.

829
00:46:58.440 --> 00:46:59.691
Let Min-jae take the lead.

830
00:46:59.775 --> 00:47:00.776
We need to dig in.

831
00:47:01.485 --> 00:47:03.695
Our pushes worked best

832
00:47:03.779 --> 00:47:06.657
right after Team Mongolia
had finished attacking.

833
00:47:07.741 --> 00:47:09.660
-Good work.
-All right, one, two, three.

834
00:47:12.454 --> 00:47:14.373
-Okay. One, two, three!
-One, two, three!

835
00:47:14.456 --> 00:47:16.208
-One, two, three!
-Get lower!

836
00:47:16.291 --> 00:47:18.710
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three!

837
00:47:18.794 --> 00:47:20.087
Get lower!

838
00:47:20.170 --> 00:47:21.421
-Okay. One, two, three.
-One, two, three.

839
00:47:21.505 --> 00:47:22.839
-Min-jae.
-One, two.

840
00:47:24.049 --> 00:47:25.092
One, two.

841
00:47:26.301 --> 00:47:27.261
One, two!

842
00:47:28.470 --> 00:47:30.097
-One, two!
-No, hold it.

843
00:47:30.180 --> 00:47:32.349
How the hell are these guys
managing to push?

844
00:47:33.058 --> 00:47:35.269
One, two, three.

845
00:47:37.271 --> 00:47:39.314
I couldn't figure out
how they were pushing so hard.

846
00:47:39.398 --> 00:47:41.400
We were also pushing
with everything we had,

847
00:47:41.984 --> 00:47:45.404
but for every step forward we took,
they took two.

848
00:47:45.487 --> 00:47:49.741
They had better technique
than we anticipated.

849
00:47:50.242 --> 00:47:51.285
One, two.

850
00:47:52.494 --> 00:47:53.620
One, two!

851
00:47:54.621 --> 00:47:56.164
-One, two!
-No, hold it.

852
00:47:57.749 --> 00:47:59.084
Enkh-Orgil, we've got to push.

853
00:47:59.167 --> 00:48:00.794
We can't just keep holding like this.

854
00:48:02.379 --> 00:48:03.630
One, two.

855
00:48:05.257 --> 00:48:07.050
No! Sung-bin, get down lower.

856
00:48:08.719 --> 00:48:11.054
No, don't face sideways, face forward!

857
00:48:12.222 --> 00:48:13.265
Okay, let's push.

858
00:48:13.348 --> 00:48:14.725
One, two, three.

859
00:48:14.808 --> 00:48:16.059
-One, two, three.
-Keep pushing!

860
00:48:16.143 --> 00:48:17.853
-Two and a half minutes!
-One, two, three.

861
00:48:22.858 --> 00:48:23.900
Whenever you're ready, Min-jae.

862
00:48:23.984 --> 00:48:26.028
Lead us off when you're ready, Min-jae.

863
00:48:26.111 --> 00:48:28.238
-One, two, three!
-Now, push.

864
00:48:28.322 --> 00:48:30.532
-One, two, three!
-Now, push.

865
00:48:30.616 --> 00:48:31.617
Doing great, guys.

866
00:48:31.700 --> 00:48:32.701
One, two, three.

867
00:48:34.244 --> 00:48:35.662
-Go again.
-One, two, three.

868
00:48:36.163 --> 00:48:38.123
Hold it out, guys.

869
00:48:38.206 --> 00:48:39.958
Whenever you're ready, Min-jae.

870
00:48:40.542 --> 00:48:41.793
-One, two, three.
-One, two, three.

871
00:48:45.172 --> 00:48:49.468
I could see in Team Mongolia's faces
that they were getting rattled.

872
00:48:50.427 --> 00:48:52.095
I knew then that we would take the win.

873
00:48:53.263 --> 00:48:54.222
Should we give it a push now?

874
00:48:54.306 --> 00:48:55.390
One, two.

875
00:49:08.945 --> 00:49:10.614
Hold it! Come on, dig in!

876
00:49:12.741 --> 00:49:14.242
Hold it! Come on, dig in!

877
00:49:14.743 --> 00:49:19.122
Team Korea came at us hard right then,
and we felt ourselves getting pushed back.

878
00:49:19.206 --> 00:49:21.208
We could feel just how strong they were.

879
00:49:21.958 --> 00:49:23.627
-Goddamn it.
-All right, hold it!

880
00:49:25.629 --> 00:49:27.089
Dulguun, abandon that and come over to us!

881
00:49:27.172 --> 00:49:29.675
Just leave it and get over here!

882
00:49:32.135 --> 00:49:34.721
We were wiped out in the middle track
and getting pushed back.

883
00:49:34.805 --> 00:49:37.349
So I told my teammates
to jump ship and come back us up.

884
00:49:41.812 --> 00:49:45.399
-Let's go, Orkhonbayar. One, two, three.
-Three.

885
00:49:51.822 --> 00:49:52.739
He's moving. I'll go.

886
00:49:55.701 --> 00:49:56.618
He's moving. I'll go.

887
00:49:57.327 --> 00:49:58.161
Come over.

888
00:50:00.414 --> 00:50:02.958
We need one more! Min-jae, push!

889
00:50:03.041 --> 00:50:04.000
Push!

890
00:50:04.084 --> 00:50:05.001
One, two!

891
00:50:06.670 --> 00:50:07.921
One, two, three!

892
00:50:10.882 --> 00:50:11.758
A minute and a half.

893
00:50:11.842 --> 00:50:14.386
Khandsuren, run over to that one.

894
00:50:15.053 --> 00:50:16.096
Go, go!

895
00:50:18.098 --> 00:50:20.058
That's it! Spread out!

896
00:50:23.729 --> 00:50:25.564
Come on! Quick!

897
00:50:25.647 --> 00:50:27.691
Go, go! Come on!

898
00:50:30.026 --> 00:50:31.194
Two, three, push!

899
00:50:31.862 --> 00:50:32.821
Go, go!

900
00:50:32.904 --> 00:50:35.574
-Hey, push! One, two, three!
-Push again. One, two, three!

901
00:50:38.076 --> 00:50:39.786
-Come on, push. One!
-Okay. One!

902
00:50:39.870 --> 00:50:41.496
Now we need Dong-hyun. Dong-hyun!

903
00:50:41.580 --> 00:50:42.998
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three!

904
00:50:48.587 --> 00:50:49.671
Get on here, Min-jae.

905
00:50:52.382 --> 00:50:54.050
Right, let's push. One, two.

906
00:50:54.134 --> 00:50:55.135
One minute.

907
00:50:56.052 --> 00:50:59.055
One, two, three, go!

908
00:50:59.139 --> 00:51:02.267
One, two, three, go!

909
00:51:02.350 --> 00:51:05.061
-One, two.
-Come on, push, you two!

910
00:51:05.145 --> 00:51:07.898
-One, two.
-Come on, push, you two!

911
00:51:07.981 --> 00:51:10.400
-Again. One, two.
-Two, three!

912
00:51:10.484 --> 00:51:12.110
One, two, three!

913
00:51:13.111 --> 00:51:15.864
Time was running out,

914
00:51:15.947 --> 00:51:19.951
so we decided to attack the center wall
since that was the most important one.

915
00:51:20.035 --> 00:51:21.119
But…

916
00:51:23.079 --> 00:51:24.164
No, no.

917
00:51:24.247 --> 00:51:25.332
One, two.

918
00:51:25.415 --> 00:51:26.625
All right, let's push now.

919
00:51:26.708 --> 00:51:28.502
One, two, three!

920
00:51:33.924 --> 00:51:36.885
Take it home!

921
00:51:36.968 --> 00:51:38.428
One, two, three!

922
00:51:43.016 --> 00:51:44.309
Goddamn it.

923
00:51:46.228 --> 00:51:47.312
We just need to hold now!

924
00:51:48.021 --> 00:51:49.564
-Hold it!
-Twenty seconds!

925
00:51:50.649 --> 00:51:52.526
-Spread out now.
-Run over to that one.

926
00:51:54.110 --> 00:51:55.362
One's coming over!

927
00:51:56.655 --> 00:51:58.990
Let's push, Min-jae. One, two, three!

928
00:52:08.291 --> 00:52:10.585
One, two!

929
00:52:10.669 --> 00:52:12.629
One, two, three!

930
00:52:12.712 --> 00:52:15.465
Three! Two! One!

931
00:52:15.549 --> 00:52:16.800
All right!

932
00:52:19.344 --> 00:52:20.387
Stop.

933
00:52:20.470 --> 00:52:21.680
Game over.

934
00:52:25.183 --> 00:52:27.227
The winner of the third round

935
00:52:27.310 --> 00:52:28.395
is Team Republic of Korea.

936
00:52:32.858 --> 00:52:34.317
Great job, guys!

937
00:52:35.443 --> 00:52:37.737
-Great job!
-Great work.

938
00:52:37.821 --> 00:52:40.240
Sung-bin, this was all you!

939
00:52:40.323 --> 00:52:41.867
This was all Sung-bin!

940
00:52:42.450 --> 00:52:43.785
Damn, Sung-bin!

941
00:52:44.369 --> 00:52:46.621
Sung-bin, you totally crushed this one!

942
00:52:47.122 --> 00:52:48.540
You did it with your sled push.

943
00:52:49.791 --> 00:52:51.668
Man, it was so tough.

944
00:52:51.751 --> 00:52:54.379
My legs were like jelly after the game.

945
00:52:55.463 --> 00:52:59.467
We'd come back from being down,
so it was such a huge relief.

946
00:53:00.385 --> 00:53:02.178
We were all ecstatic.

947
00:53:04.389 --> 00:53:07.809
Team Republic of Korea's
two strongest walls

948
00:53:08.393 --> 00:53:10.645
were Kim Min-jae and Yun Sung-bin.

949
00:53:11.187 --> 00:53:14.733
All it took was one big shove from Min-jae
for Team Mongolia to fall apart.

950
00:53:14.816 --> 00:53:16.985
There's a reason he's a Cheonhajangsa.

951
00:53:19.070 --> 00:53:21.072
Man, we really showed them…

952
00:53:22.198 --> 00:53:23.825
the power of South Korea.

953
00:53:24.326 --> 00:53:26.536
-It's all right, guys.
-It's fine, it's fine.

954
00:53:27.412 --> 00:53:29.247
It's all right.

955
00:53:30.081 --> 00:53:31.541
We got pushed way too easily, right?

956
00:53:33.084 --> 00:53:35.128
We had it but blew it.

957
00:53:35.921 --> 00:53:39.007
We spread ourselves too thin
by fighting them on too many fronts.

958
00:53:39.591 --> 00:53:44.846
We lost the first game,
but I told my team not to sweat it.

959
00:53:45.347 --> 00:53:46.806
We still had two more to go,

960
00:53:46.890 --> 00:53:48.975
so we could crush it in those.

961
00:53:58.318 --> 00:54:01.863
The final quest of Physical: Asia.

962
00:54:01.947 --> 00:54:04.324
As the loser of the first game,

963
00:54:05.408 --> 00:54:07.869
Team Mongolia will choose the second game.

964
00:54:08.370 --> 00:54:09.788
The remaining games are…

965
00:54:13.208 --> 00:54:14.542
the infinite tail tag match

966
00:54:15.794 --> 00:54:17.420
and the iron ball dragging match.

967
00:54:23.593 --> 00:54:26.262
Right, so tail tagging
or iron ball dragging?

968
00:54:29.683 --> 00:54:30.642
I wonder what they'll pick.

969
00:54:31.309 --> 00:54:32.894
We're definitely stronger than them.

970
00:54:33.395 --> 00:54:35.939
I figured the iron ball dragging
would be better for us

971
00:54:36.022 --> 00:54:38.191
because the wall-pushing match
was all about strength and we won.

972
00:54:38.775 --> 00:54:42.112
I doubted they'd pick
another strength game,

973
00:54:42.195 --> 00:54:43.697
and assumed they'd choose
the infinite tail tag match.

974
00:54:44.572 --> 00:54:47.033
What do we do?
Is it all over if we lose this?

975
00:54:47.117 --> 00:54:48.159
Yeah.

976
00:54:50.203 --> 00:54:54.082
I'd say they're better runners than us.

977
00:54:54.165 --> 00:54:55.000
You're right.

978
00:54:55.083 --> 00:54:57.919
You saw those guys
on the treadmill, right?

979
00:54:58.962 --> 00:55:01.923
There was a running challenge
to win a privilege,

980
00:55:02.007 --> 00:55:04.551
and Team Korea came first in that.

981
00:55:04.634 --> 00:55:07.012
They were beasts on the treadmill.

982
00:55:08.680 --> 00:55:10.724
-The iron ball would be better.
-Should we go with that then?

983
00:55:10.807 --> 00:55:12.017
But in the game just now,

984
00:55:12.976 --> 00:55:14.477
we went toe-to-toe with them and lost.

985
00:55:16.229 --> 00:55:20.442
I thought hard about
which match my team would be better at.

986
00:55:21.901 --> 00:55:24.404
The strategy meeting is over.

987
00:55:26.322 --> 00:55:30.201
Team leader of Mongolia,
Orkhonbayar Bayarsaikhan,

988
00:55:30.285 --> 00:55:32.454
please choose the second game.

989
00:55:34.497 --> 00:55:35.331
What will it be?

990
00:55:42.464 --> 00:55:45.175
We'll choose the iron ball dragging match.

991
00:55:52.307 --> 00:55:55.060
We'll choose the iron ball dragging match.

992
00:55:57.062 --> 00:55:59.731
That's good. That's good.

993
00:56:00.315 --> 00:56:02.567
I was both anxious and excited.

994
00:56:03.234 --> 00:56:06.780
I knew weight class
and body weight were important,

995
00:56:06.863 --> 00:56:10.825
and Team Mongolia
had two pretty hefty players.

996
00:56:11.409 --> 00:56:12.660
That was what worried me.

997
00:56:12.744 --> 00:56:15.371
You know how they say
you can't beat weight class.

998
00:56:15.872 --> 00:56:18.625
Since Team Mongolia was bigger than us,
I knew that in terms of strength,

999
00:56:19.834 --> 00:56:21.211
they'd be challenging.

1000
00:56:21.836 --> 00:56:23.171
Here we go, another head-to-head.

1001
00:56:23.671 --> 00:56:24.756
Yeah, here we go.

1002
00:56:25.882 --> 00:56:27.175
Should we go with the iron ball?

1003
00:56:27.258 --> 00:56:28.802
Yeah, we can't outrun them.

1004
00:56:29.302 --> 00:56:30.470
But in the game just now,

1005
00:56:31.429 --> 00:56:32.972
we went toe-to-toe with them and lost.

1006
00:56:33.056 --> 00:56:36.643
That wasn't about strength or weight,
it was just bad strategy.

1007
00:56:36.726 --> 00:56:38.937
We could've won,
and we're going to win this.

1008
00:56:39.521 --> 00:56:42.273
In terms of strength,
we had an edge in this match too.

1009
00:56:42.357 --> 00:56:45.527
I figured we might as well go all out
and prove our strength.

1010
00:56:45.610 --> 00:56:48.655
And I felt more confident
knowing that it'd be a strength game.

1011
00:56:48.738 --> 00:56:50.532
I was confident we'd win.

1012
00:56:50.615 --> 00:56:55.370
If we won the second round
and wore out Team Korea in the process,

1013
00:56:55.453 --> 00:57:00.083
we'd have the advantage
in the infinite tail tag match too.

1014
00:57:01.709 --> 00:57:03.253
Physical: Asia.

1015
00:57:03.878 --> 00:57:06.714
The second game of the final quest

1016
00:57:07.632 --> 00:57:09.467
is the iron ball dragging match.

1017
00:57:09.968 --> 00:57:11.594
All right, here we go.

1018
00:57:12.720 --> 00:57:14.097
Let's finish this off.

1019
00:57:14.180 --> 00:57:15.515
Let's finish this thing off.

1020
00:57:22.480 --> 00:57:24.566
That actually looks like a lump of iron.

1021
00:57:25.191 --> 00:57:27.360
It looks quite heavy.

1022
00:57:28.361 --> 00:57:31.281
Are we supposed to
attach that to ourselves?

1023
00:57:31.865 --> 00:57:34.909
There were about
four more iron balls on the side.

1024
00:57:34.993 --> 00:57:38.788
I wondered if we were supposed to
haul all of them.

1025
00:57:38.872 --> 00:57:42.041
In the iron ball dragging match,
all six members

1026
00:57:42.625 --> 00:57:45.545
must drag the iron balls
harnessed to their bodies

1027
00:57:47.172 --> 00:57:49.132
to reach the flag at the finish point

1028
00:57:49.632 --> 00:57:52.010
and knock it down with their hands.

1029
00:57:53.720 --> 00:57:56.347
We'd look like dogs leashed up.

1030
00:57:58.475 --> 00:58:01.060
Judging by how many footholds there are,
it'll be just barely manageable.

1031
00:58:01.686 --> 00:58:04.981
There are a total of
five footholds on the track.

1032
00:58:08.276 --> 00:58:10.361
The time limit is three minutes.

1033
00:58:11.279 --> 00:58:15.575
If time runs out
before you knock down the flag, you fail.

1034
00:58:17.035 --> 00:58:20.163
The game will consist of
a total of five rounds.

1035
00:58:21.164 --> 00:58:22.332
In each round,

1036
00:58:22.415 --> 00:58:25.126
the weight of the iron ball
will increase proportionally

1037
00:58:25.210 --> 00:58:26.586
to each team's total body weight.

1038
00:58:27.504 --> 00:58:28.963
-So that's five weight increases.
-Yeah.

1039
00:58:29.464 --> 00:58:32.175
Team Korea's average was higher than ours,

1040
00:58:32.258 --> 00:58:35.470
which meant that their iron balls

1041
00:58:35.553 --> 00:58:38.932
would be heavier than ours.

1042
00:58:39.015 --> 00:58:40.934
That was advantageous for us.

1043
00:58:53.738 --> 00:58:57.951
The two countries
will take turns in each round.

1044
00:58:58.034 --> 00:58:59.244
ORDER OF PLAY WAS DETERMINED
BY DRAWING LOTS

1045
00:58:59.827 --> 00:59:01.996
If both countries succeed
in a given round,

1046
00:59:02.080 --> 00:59:04.499
they will have a rematch
in the following round.

1047
00:59:04.999 --> 00:59:06.209
Interesting.

1048
00:59:07.502 --> 00:59:11.548
If either country fails, the game…

1049
00:59:12.840 --> 00:59:13.967
will end immediately.

1050
00:59:15.760 --> 00:59:17.887
If those guys fail a round,
we absolutely have to succeed.

1051
00:59:18.888 --> 00:59:20.473
If there is no winner after five rounds,

1052
00:59:20.974 --> 00:59:23.226
the countries will compete simultaneously,

1053
00:59:24.060 --> 00:59:28.231
and whoever knocks down their flag first
will be the winner.

1054
00:59:31.985 --> 00:59:33.570
Mongolian warriors,

1055
00:59:33.653 --> 00:59:36.531
you certainly proved your power
in the first match.

1056
00:59:37.031 --> 00:59:39.826
But no matter how strong
our opponents are,

1057
00:59:39.909 --> 00:59:41.494
we Koreans never give up,

1058
00:59:41.578 --> 00:59:45.123
and turn things around
with perseverance and grit.

1059
00:59:45.206 --> 00:59:47.625
That's why we'll be the ultimate victors,

1060
00:59:47.709 --> 00:59:49.335
and I can guarantee you

1061
00:59:49.419 --> 00:59:53.006
that this will be the final match
of Physical: Asia.

1062
00:59:54.173 --> 00:59:56.259
We'll make this game
more interesting for you.

1063
00:59:56.342 --> 00:59:58.511
Don't get too comfortable, guys.

1064
00:59:59.929 --> 01:00:02.515
We have no room for any more losses,

1065
01:00:02.599 --> 01:00:04.350
so we're going to give it our all.

1066
01:00:05.768 --> 01:00:07.437
Physical: Asia.

1067
01:00:08.187 --> 01:00:10.356
The second game of the final quest.

1068
01:00:13.026 --> 01:00:16.154
The first round
of the iron ball dragging match.

1069
01:00:16.654 --> 01:00:18.740
First up is Team Mongolia.

1070
01:00:19.490 --> 01:00:21.159
Why is the bökh guy fourth in line?

1071
01:00:21.242 --> 01:00:22.327
-Yeah.
-What?

1072
01:00:22.410 --> 01:00:24.454
I noticed that and thought it was odd too.

1073
01:00:25.163 --> 01:00:27.832
We thought Orkhonbayar
would be in the middle,

1074
01:00:27.915 --> 01:00:28.958
but he wasn't.

1075
01:00:29.042 --> 01:00:32.337
He was near the end,
which was really unexpected.

1076
01:00:33.129 --> 01:00:35.340
Adiyasuren was in the middle.

1077
01:00:35.423 --> 01:00:37.300
Dulguun was also in the middle.

1078
01:00:37.800 --> 01:00:40.178
I wondered what their game plan was.

1079
01:00:41.137 --> 01:00:44.515
Since I'm the tallest,
I'd get to the finish point first.

1080
01:00:44.599 --> 01:00:45.808
Dulguun, reach up like this.

1081
01:00:46.476 --> 01:00:48.269
-I can reach way higher than you.
-Exactly.

1082
01:00:48.353 --> 01:00:51.481
We put him in the center
because he has the longest limbs.

1083
01:00:51.564 --> 01:00:54.734
It'd work to our advantage
since he'd get to the finish point first.

1084
01:00:54.817 --> 01:00:58.988
And then Adiyasuren and I
were on either side of him

1085
01:00:59.072 --> 01:01:00.114
to take on the weight.

1086
01:01:00.198 --> 01:01:04.285
Our goal was to distribute
our strength equally on each side.

1087
01:01:08.039 --> 01:01:09.749
Let's show them.

1088
01:01:09.832 --> 01:01:10.875
Yeah, let's bring it!

1089
01:01:13.044 --> 01:01:13.920
Let's see.

1090
01:01:14.671 --> 01:01:16.506
Let's see how they go about this.

1091
01:01:16.589 --> 01:01:17.674
Stand by.

1092
01:01:25.890 --> 01:01:26.891
Ready…

1093
01:01:28.768 --> 01:01:31.229
We have three minutes,
so there's no need to run.

1094
01:01:34.899 --> 01:01:36.776
Don't run. Take it slow and steady.

1095
01:01:36.859 --> 01:01:38.778
Don't run. Take it slow and steady.

1096
01:01:38.861 --> 01:01:40.279
Right, take it easy.

1097
01:01:41.030 --> 01:01:41.948
They're going slowly.

1098
01:01:42.448 --> 01:01:43.741
I think they want a steady pull.

1099
01:01:44.992 --> 01:01:47.203
Since it was only the first round,

1100
01:01:47.286 --> 01:01:51.165
we decided to take it steady
to get a feel for it.

1101
01:01:57.213 --> 01:01:58.297
Slowly.

1102
01:02:00.675 --> 01:02:01.759
Slowly.

1103
01:02:03.261 --> 01:02:04.846
It wasn't that heavy.

1104
01:02:04.929 --> 01:02:06.806
The first round felt pretty easy.

1105
01:02:08.808 --> 01:02:11.185
I didn't even pull,
and we're already here.

1106
01:02:11.269 --> 01:02:12.437
Stop.

1107
01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:13.896
Game over.

1108
01:02:13.980 --> 01:02:15.022
The first one looks easy.

1109
01:02:15.106 --> 01:02:16.983
-Yeah, since it's only 20% of the weight.
-Right.

1110
01:02:17.066 --> 01:02:18.276
It's probably pretty light.

1111
01:02:18.359 --> 01:02:20.319
Team Mongolia has succeeded.

1112
01:02:21.320 --> 01:02:23.990
The first round
of the iron ball dragging match.

1113
01:02:24.490 --> 01:02:26.075
Next up is Team Republic of Korea.

1114
01:02:26.993 --> 01:02:29.245
We should just try
and get a feel for it too.

1115
01:02:29.328 --> 01:02:32.373
-We'll all need to pull together.
-Right.

1116
01:02:32.457 --> 01:02:35.001
This is pretty much
something I do all the time,

1117
01:02:35.084 --> 01:02:39.213
so I knew I wouldn't hold my team back.

1118
01:02:39.297 --> 01:02:41.549
Let's decide on our positions.
Who's in the center?

1119
01:02:41.632 --> 01:02:43.176
-Min-jae.
-Come to the center, Min-jae.

1120
01:02:43.259 --> 01:02:45.178
Min-jae, come to the center.
Yeah, this is the way.

1121
01:02:45.261 --> 01:02:47.555
You guys need to be on each end.

1122
01:02:48.306 --> 01:02:50.767
Because there were six of us,

1123
01:02:50.850 --> 01:02:53.478
the force could spread a bit in a Y-shape.

1124
01:02:53.561 --> 01:02:57.023
So we decided to put our strongest players
in the center.

1125
01:02:57.106 --> 01:03:00.151
Our plan was to use our strongest players
as our anchor point.

1126
01:03:01.194 --> 01:03:04.906
Let's see how they do it
and what their technique is.

1127
01:03:06.657 --> 01:03:08.659
Their ball is 10 kg heavier than ours.

1128
01:03:10.369 --> 01:03:11.412
Stand by.

1129
01:03:12.330 --> 01:03:14.248
-Let's do this.
-Let's get a feel for it.

1130
01:03:14.332 --> 01:03:15.208
Ready…

1131
01:03:32.183 --> 01:03:34.101
It's easy so far.

1132
01:03:34.185 --> 01:03:36.270
Is this it? It's really light.

1133
01:03:37.355 --> 01:03:40.024
I could tell why
Team Mongolia didn't break a sweat.

1134
01:03:40.608 --> 01:03:42.860
It looked like Team Korea

1135
01:03:42.944 --> 01:03:46.072
were exerting themselves
about as much as we had.

1136
01:03:48.991 --> 01:03:50.535
All right, grab it.

1137
01:03:53.079 --> 01:03:54.747
-That was too easy.
-Yeah, that was good.

1138
01:03:54.831 --> 01:03:55.790
Stop.

1139
01:03:55.873 --> 01:03:56.958
Game over.

1140
01:03:57.625 --> 01:04:00.169
Team Republic of Korea has succeeded.

1141
01:04:08.469 --> 01:04:09.929
The second round.

1142
01:04:10.012 --> 01:04:11.806
First up is Team Mongolia.

1143
01:04:12.807 --> 01:04:14.934
-Right, left.
-One, two.

1144
01:04:15.017 --> 01:04:18.187
-Right, left, right, left.
-One, two, one, two.

1145
01:04:19.105 --> 01:04:23.943
The weight in the second round didn't feel
any different from the first round.

1146
01:04:26.195 --> 01:04:27.905
Team Mongolia has succeeded.

1147
01:04:27.989 --> 01:04:29.198
The second round.

1148
01:04:29.282 --> 01:04:30.950
Next up is Team Republic of Korea.

1149
01:04:32.118 --> 01:04:34.120
Quick steps, quick steps.

1150
01:04:36.831 --> 01:04:38.666
This is great.

1151
01:04:38.749 --> 01:04:40.710
The second round was also easy.

1152
01:04:41.419 --> 01:04:42.253
It was a piece of cake.

1153
01:04:42.336 --> 01:04:44.338
Team Republic of Korea has succeeded.

1154
01:04:45.423 --> 01:04:47.592
The third round
of the iron ball dragging match.

1155
01:04:47.675 --> 01:04:49.093
First up is Team Mongolia.

1156
01:04:49.176 --> 01:04:51.137
One, two.

1157
01:04:51.220 --> 01:04:52.847
One, two.

1158
01:04:52.930 --> 01:04:54.140
Lower your body.

1159
01:04:54.223 --> 01:04:55.182
Lower your body.

1160
01:04:55.975 --> 01:04:56.809
Let's go.

1161
01:05:04.483 --> 01:05:06.027
They're struggling to crawl.

1162
01:05:06.110 --> 01:05:07.987
Leaning forward gives you more leverage.

1163
01:05:08.529 --> 01:05:11.657
The weight got heavy in the third round,

1164
01:05:11.741 --> 01:05:16.120
so I suggested
that we try crawling together.

1165
01:05:16.203 --> 01:05:17.413
You just need to touch it.

1166
01:05:19.206 --> 01:05:20.875
Team Mongolia has succeeded.

1167
01:05:21.667 --> 01:05:23.336
You need to lean forward for leverage.

1168
01:05:23.419 --> 01:05:24.462
Absolutely.

1169
01:05:24.545 --> 01:05:25.922
The third round.

1170
01:05:26.005 --> 01:05:27.965
Next up is Team Republic of Korea.

1171
01:05:28.049 --> 01:05:30.801
One, two, one, two.

1172
01:05:30.885 --> 01:05:31.761
Here we go.

1173
01:05:31.844 --> 01:05:32.929
-All right.
-Get down.

1174
01:05:33.554 --> 01:05:37.099
We also figured
we had to lower our center of gravity.

1175
01:05:37.183 --> 01:05:39.310
-One, two.
-One, two.

1176
01:05:39.393 --> 01:05:40.645
They're doing what we did.

1177
01:05:40.728 --> 01:05:41.854
Yeah, they are.

1178
01:05:43.856 --> 01:05:47.735
The third round was when
we started to feel the weight a bit.

1179
01:05:48.235 --> 01:05:49.320
Okay, hit it.

1180
01:05:50.279 --> 01:05:52.239
Team Republic of Korea has succeeded.

1181
01:05:52.865 --> 01:05:54.367
The weight will now be increased.

1182
01:05:55.701 --> 01:05:58.329
I think it'll get pretty tough
starting with this round.

1183
01:05:58.412 --> 01:05:59.372
Is it three balls?

1184
01:05:59.455 --> 01:06:00.790
Shit, it's three.

1185
01:06:00.873 --> 01:06:02.750
It's three balls now,
so it'll get tougher now.

1186
01:06:02.833 --> 01:06:04.669
Yeah, it's going to be quite tough.

1187
01:06:04.752 --> 01:06:06.379
I was worried.

1188
01:06:06.462 --> 01:06:08.297
It was ramping up more than I thought.

1189
01:06:08.381 --> 01:06:13.552
The fourth round was going to be
really tough and require a lot of stamina.

1190
01:06:14.053 --> 01:06:16.555
The fourth round
of the iron ball dragging match.

1191
01:06:16.639 --> 01:06:18.307
First up is Team Mongolia.

1192
01:06:18.808 --> 01:06:21.310
Let's start crawling
as soon as we reach the first foothold.

1193
01:06:21.394 --> 01:06:23.354
We'll need to cling
and dig into the footholds.

1194
01:06:23.437 --> 01:06:24.647
Try to shovel into them with your hands.

1195
01:06:24.730 --> 01:06:27.024
Yeah, use the footholds for leverage.

1196
01:06:27.525 --> 01:06:28.484
Stand by.

1197
01:06:33.531 --> 01:06:35.992
I really hope they fail this round.

1198
01:06:36.075 --> 01:06:38.536
If they fail, that's our opportunity.

1199
01:06:38.619 --> 01:06:39.829
Ready…

1200
01:06:39.912 --> 01:06:43.416
I have confidence in ourselves
that we can get through every weight.

1201
01:06:44.625 --> 01:06:46.335
One, two, three.

1202
01:06:47.253 --> 01:06:49.797
One, two, three. Get down.

1203
01:06:49.880 --> 01:06:51.549
One, two.

1204
01:06:51.632 --> 01:06:52.883
One, two.

1205
01:06:56.929 --> 01:06:58.389
I panicked at that moment.

1206
01:06:58.973 --> 01:07:03.310
It was heavier and tougher
than I expected.

1207
01:07:07.314 --> 01:07:08.733
-It must be quite heavy.
-Yeah.

1208
01:07:08.816 --> 01:07:09.775
It's a lot harder now.

1209
01:07:10.443 --> 01:07:12.862
-One, two.
-One, two.

1210
01:07:12.945 --> 01:07:15.364
-One, two.
-One, two.

1211
01:07:18.325 --> 01:07:20.786
One, two.

1212
01:07:20.870 --> 01:07:21.787
That's it.

1213
01:07:22.413 --> 01:07:23.330
That's it.

1214
01:07:26.542 --> 01:07:28.419
The fourth round
was when it got really tough.

1215
01:07:28.502 --> 01:07:31.505
We crawled along very slowly,
barely clinging on to the footholds.

1216
01:07:33.966 --> 01:07:36.927
-One, two.
-Reach for it!

1217
01:07:37.011 --> 01:07:38.304
Wow, they're moving forward.

1218
01:07:46.896 --> 01:07:47.980
Reach for it!

1219
01:07:52.777 --> 01:07:56.489
We couldn't keep our movements in rhythm
when we were crawling.

1220
01:07:56.572 --> 01:07:58.491
We couldn't balance our power well.

1221
01:07:59.533 --> 01:08:03.079
It was key for everyone to pull forward
with the exact same force,

1222
01:08:03.162 --> 01:08:04.997
but that wasn't so easy to pull off.

1223
01:08:14.632 --> 01:08:17.343
-One, two, three!
-Go!

1224
01:08:17.426 --> 01:08:18.385
Hit it.

1225
01:08:18.469 --> 01:08:19.804
Make a stretch for it!

1226
01:08:26.685 --> 01:08:28.270
-Game over.
-Twenty-nine seconds.

1227
01:08:28.854 --> 01:08:30.022
-It's getting so heavy.
-Yeah.

1228
01:08:30.106 --> 01:08:32.108
Team Mongolia has succeeded.

1229
01:08:37.905 --> 01:08:40.157
We're not pulling together.

1230
01:08:40.241 --> 01:08:42.326
-Right.
-That's our problem right now.

1231
01:08:42.409 --> 01:08:44.829
-We're all doing our own thing.
-We should count off as we go.

1232
01:08:44.912 --> 01:08:47.164
-Yeah, we need to move together.
-We're not coordinated.

1233
01:08:47.248 --> 01:08:49.125
We're each just going at our own pace.

1234
01:08:49.208 --> 01:08:51.252
Someone's got to keep us in line,
Orkhonbayar.

1235
01:08:51.335 --> 01:08:52.795
That's not the way to do it.

1236
01:08:52.878 --> 01:08:55.673
They should've shouted,
"One, two! One, two!"

1237
01:08:55.756 --> 01:08:57.299
That way, you move in perfect rhythm.

1238
01:08:57.383 --> 01:09:01.220
We need to coordinate our steps
and all go at the same pace.

1239
01:09:01.804 --> 01:09:04.265
The fourth round
of the iron ball dragging match.

1240
01:09:04.348 --> 01:09:06.475
Next up is Team Republic of Korea.

1241
01:09:06.559 --> 01:09:07.393
Let's do this.

1242
01:09:07.476 --> 01:09:09.019
-Match the speed of those next to you.
-Okay.

1243
01:09:09.103 --> 01:09:10.187
Stand by.

1244
01:09:10.938 --> 01:09:12.148
-Here they go.
-Yeah.

1245
01:09:12.231 --> 01:09:13.440
Let's watch them carefully.

1246
01:09:13.524 --> 01:09:16.277
I was hoping Team Korea would screw up.

1247
01:09:16.360 --> 01:09:20.030
I thought maybe
they wouldn't be able to manage it.

1248
01:09:20.114 --> 01:09:21.198
Ready…

1249
01:09:22.241 --> 01:09:24.451
We couldn't afford to mess this up.

1250
01:09:24.535 --> 01:09:27.329
I tried to keep myself focused
on the task at hand.

1251
01:09:29.957 --> 01:09:32.168
Hook your feet against the foothold.
That's it.

1252
01:09:32.251 --> 01:09:33.878
That's it.

1253
01:09:33.961 --> 01:09:35.171
-One, two.
-One, two.

1254
01:09:39.216 --> 01:09:40.551
-One, two.
-One, two.

