01:35:18.421 --> 01:35:19.964
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three!

1739
01:35:20.047 --> 01:35:22.383
I feel like I'm not strong on my own…

1740
01:35:24.969 --> 01:35:27.138
but I become stronger
when I'm with the team.

1741
01:35:27.763 --> 01:35:28.973
Republic of Korea!

1742
01:35:29.056 --> 01:35:30.224
Let's go!

1743
01:35:30.766 --> 01:35:36.439
I think that bond is what propelled us
this far to the victory.

1744
01:35:37.982 --> 01:35:39.984
Coming together as a team…

1745
01:35:40.067 --> 01:35:43.696
-One, two, three!
-One, two, three!

1746
01:35:43.779 --> 01:35:45.781
…with every passing moment…

1747
01:35:45.865 --> 01:35:48.826
-We're strong.
-It's a mental game now.

1748
01:35:48.909 --> 01:35:50.953
…and pushing through every hurdle,

1749
01:35:52.580 --> 01:35:54.206
I felt we were becoming stronger.

1750
01:35:54.290 --> 01:35:58.627
The last one hanging match

1751
01:35:58.711 --> 01:36:04.675
completely wrecked me
both mentally and physically.

1752
01:36:07.219 --> 01:36:10.139
My confidence
took a really big hit from it,

1753
01:36:10.222 --> 01:36:12.016
and I realized I had a long way to go.

1754
01:36:12.600 --> 01:36:13.476
I'm so sorry.

1755
01:36:13.559 --> 01:36:15.478
-Don't apologize.
-Hey, you did your best.

1756
01:36:15.561 --> 01:36:17.980
You gave it everything you got.
You did amazing.

1757
01:36:19.523 --> 01:36:22.735
But my teammates cheered me on

1758
01:36:22.818 --> 01:36:25.488
and gave me incredible support
through their words

1759
01:36:25.571 --> 01:36:27.406
and by just being there for me.

1760
01:36:27.490 --> 01:36:30.284
It's helped me grow stronger
and more resilient.

1761
01:36:34.788 --> 01:36:36.499
Min-jae, you did great.

1762
01:36:36.582 --> 01:36:38.918
You were amazing.

1763
01:36:39.877 --> 01:36:41.170
You did great.

1764
01:36:41.253 --> 01:36:43.422
I feel like this has been a life lesson,

1765
01:36:44.423 --> 01:36:47.676
so all I can really say is thank you.

1766
01:36:48.260 --> 01:36:49.845
You're almost there, Min-jae!

1767
01:36:49.929 --> 01:36:52.097
I've learned not to give up…

1768
01:36:55.267 --> 01:36:58.395
and to give it my all.

1769
01:37:00.481 --> 01:37:03.609
-Great job, guys!
-Nice!

1770
01:37:05.736 --> 01:37:08.280
I'll be returning
to the sand mat of ssireum,

1771
01:37:08.864 --> 01:37:11.492
but the sand I walked on in Physical: Asia

1772
01:37:12.076 --> 01:37:14.745
will remain an unforgettable memory.

1773
01:37:16.038 --> 01:37:21.544
In Season 2, I experienced this joy alone.

1774
01:37:21.627 --> 01:37:26.340
But this time,
I get to share it with my teammates,

1775
01:37:27.341 --> 01:37:28.676
and I'm really happy about that.

1776
01:37:47.903 --> 01:37:53.951
Sharing this win with my teammates

1777
01:37:54.034 --> 01:37:58.038
and sharing the experience
has been a true joy.

1778
01:37:58.122 --> 01:37:59.081
Republic of Korea!

1779
01:37:59.164 --> 01:38:01.041
-Proud and strong!
-Proud and strong!

1780
01:38:03.168 --> 01:38:07.006
We, Team Republic of Korea,
protected our torsos…

1781
01:38:13.012 --> 01:38:14.346
and did our flag proud.

1782
01:38:18.350 --> 01:38:20.311
Physical: Asia.

1783
01:38:21.645 --> 01:38:26.358
Throughout the competition,
we explored various physiques

1784
01:38:27.526 --> 01:38:30.070
in search of the most perfect one.

1785
01:38:32.072 --> 01:38:36.619
Our quest to find
the pinnacle of physique,

1786
01:38:38.537 --> 01:38:42.541
regardless of sex, age, or race…

1787
01:38:44.668 --> 01:38:46.128
will continue.

